  "details": "<p>According to Livy, the <em>tribus Scaptia</em> was organised when Q. Publilius Philo and Sp. Postumius were censors. The name derives from Scaptia, a town in Latium, the location of which is no longer known.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A later rural tribe of ancient Rome, which was established in 332 B.C. ",
